      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "   \nStarting with the given equation \\(x^2 - 6x + y^2 + 2y + 6 = 0\\), we will rewrite it in the standard form of a circle's equation, \\((x - h)^2 + (y - k)^2 = r^2\\).\n\nFirst, let's complete the square for the \\(x\\) terms:\n\n\\[x^2 - 6x\\]\n\nTo complete the square, we add and subtract \\(\\left(\\frac{6}{2}\\right)^2 = 9\\):\n\n\\[x^2 - 6x + 9 - 9\\]\n\nThis gives us:\n\n\\[\\left(x - 3\\right)^2 - 9\\]\n\nNext, we complete the square for the \\(y\\) terms:\n\n\\[y^2 + 2y\\]\n\nSimilarly, add and subtract \\(\\left(\\frac{2}{2}\\right)^2 = 1\\):\n\n\\[y^2 + 2y + 1 - 1\\]\n\nThis gives us:\n\n\\[(y + 1)^2 - 1\\]\n\nPutting it all together, we have:\n\n\\[\\left(x - 3\\right)^2 - 9 + \\left(y + 1\\right)^2 - 1 + 6 = 0\\]\n\nSimplify the constants:\n\n\\[\\left(x - 3\\right)^2 + \\left(y + 1\\right)^2 - 4 = 0\\]\n\nAdding \\(4\\) to both sides:\n\n\\[\\left(x - 3\\right)^2 + \\left(y + 1\\right)^2 = 4\\]\n\nThe equation is now in the standard form of a circle's equation. The center of the circle is \\((3, -1)\\) and the radius \\(r\\) is:\n\n\\[r^2 = 4\\]\n\nTherefore, the radius:\n\n\\[r = \\boxed{2}\\]",
